**12. Lazy Assertion Messages**

```java
class LazyMessageTest {

    @Test
    void testWithLazyMessages() {
        String actual = someOperation();

        // Message is only constructed if assertion fails
        assertEquals("expected", actual, 
            () -> expensiveMessageConstruction(actual));

        // Useful for complex message building
        assertTrue(validate(actual),
            () -> String.format("Validation failed for input '%s' with result %s",
                actual, getDetailedResult()));
    }

    private String expensiveMessageConstruction(String actual) {
        // Imagine this does logging, API calls, etc.
        return "Expected 'expected' but was '" + actual + "'";
    }
}
